  "description": "Heights with a split, a Gaussian beam, stacked mirrors, an iris and a periscope. L1 (785 nm, 1.5 mm, 20 mW) at 78 mm, 3 mm above BS1 (75): both branches stay at 78. Transmitted: M_B (300 mm) and M_A (75) stand at one place; M_A, at the beam's height, is hit, and M_B, at the very point of the hit, is not a pass; the beam goes up to IRIS (75, opening 4), which blocks it in height (|dz| 3 > 2). Reflected: it passes under M_P (200, dz -122); P1 (entrance 75, exit 300, along its +x) lifts it to 303 (dz +3 at both ends), a 225 mm run; M_UP (300) turns it to +x; it crosses the surfaces of M_NM (75) and M_NM2 (300) 7.1 mm beyond their edges, and only M_NM2, at its height, is a near miss (expected_misses); D_S (300, aperture 6) is hit with dz +3 = half its aperture, path_mm 1375, d = 1.757676 mm (zR = 2251.141 mm): its spot reaches 0.878838 mm past its upper edge.",
